<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Sept 7.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Sept 7.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended September 7:</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   193	   0.47     431000  83.18    12.70</p>
<p>State Bank	   280	   0.68     258900  72.49    12.66</p>
<p>Reliance	     205	   0.47     226750  46.48    11.95</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    250	   0.58     154250  38.56    12.10</p>
<p>Tata Power	   157	   0.39     225250  35.36    12.95</p>
<p>ACC		   2130	   5.38	13460  28.67    13.17</p>
<p>ITC		    295	   0.10	82100  24.22     1.77</p>
<p>Tata Chem	    210	   0.51	55550  11.67    12.66</p>
<p>Gujarat Ambuja     315	   0.70	36100  11.37    11.59</p>
<p>Colgate		255	   0.36	35650   9.09     7.36</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 11.38  percent on an annualised basis against 12.16 percent in the previous carry forward account ended August 31.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
